# Routing

- **All routes are defined in `src/App.tsx`** using React Router.
- Do not create separate router config files unless the user explicitly asks later.
- Each route renders a page from `src/pages/`.
- `App.tsx` must stay thin: providers + `<Routes>` / `<Route>` only — no page UI.

```tsx
// src/App.tsx — pattern
import { BrowserRouter, Routes, Route } from 'react-router-dom';
import { HomePage } from './pages/HomePage';
import { UsersPage } from './pages/UsersPage';

export default function App() {
  return (
    <BrowserRouter>
      <Routes>
        <Route path="/" element={<HomePage />} />
        <Route path="/users" element={<UsersPage />} />
      </Routes>
    </BrowserRouter>
  );
}
```

If the user proposes routes elsewhere, explain they must stay in `App.tsx` and redirect the change there.
